4,1,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,George,,Hello everyone. It seems our current arrangement isn't working as well as it used to. I think we need a more structured system to avoid any further tension between us. What do you all think?,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I agree, George. The current informality is creating unnecessary friction. We need a system that is clear and sustainable for everyone involved to avoid these breakdowns in the future.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree. It's become difficult to rely on the car lately. I think we need a system that ensures the vehicle is actually available and in a usable condition when we need it.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We should establish a clear framework. To make it fair, we need to understand the actual costs and usage patterns so no one is unintentionally subsidizing others.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Minato,,"I agree with everyone. I think it would be nice if we could all be honest and clear about how we use the car and the money, so nobody feels sad or worried.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,George,,"To make a fair decision, we should look at the facts. I suggest we examine the hours of use recorded in the diary and what two other car-sharing households said to see how they handle things.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"That sounds reasonable. To complement that, I suggest we look into the hours of use recorded in the diary and the spell of checking each other's figures to see where the administrative friction lies.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Victoria,,I think we should look at the state of the car at handover and the mechanic's remarks at the last service. We need to understand why the vehicle's condition has been so inconsistent.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"I think we need a clearer picture of the finances. I suggest looking into last year's fuel receipts and last year's tax, insurance and parking papers to see the actual overhead.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Minato,,I want to know the real numbers too. I think we should look at last year's fuel receipts and the month's trial of recording every run to see who is driving the most.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,George,,"It seems we have a good variety of data points to cover. By looking at both the usage logs and external examples, we can find a balance that preserves our friendship while staying organized.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"Indeed. By analyzing both the actual usage and the time spent on administration, we can identify the specific bottlenecks. This will allow us to build a system that minimizes stress and maximizes efficiency.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I believe that focusing on the physical state of the car is just as important as the numbers. If we don't address the reliability of the vehicle, no amount of scheduling will solve the problem.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree that the car's condition matters, but we must ensure the financial burden is distributed correctly. If we ignore the overhead and fuel costs, we risk an unfair arrangement.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Minato,,"I think everyone's ideas are important. If we look at the money and the car's condition together, we can make a plan that is fair and makes everyone happy.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,George,,I believe we are in agreement. Let's proceed with these investigations. I will look into the hours of use recorded in the diary and what two other car-sharing households said. I hope this helps us avoid future conflict.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Toshio,,I will look into the hours of use recorded in the diary and the spell of checking each other's figures. I want to see exactly how much time we are wasting on coordination.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I will look into the state of the car at handover and the mechanic's remarks at the last service. I want to ensure we address the reliability of the vehicle for everyone.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will look into last year's fuel receipts and last year's tax, insurance and parking papers. I want to ensure we have a precise understanding of the total costs before we decide on a split.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Minato,,I will look into last year's fuel receipts and the month's trial of recording every run. I hope this helps us see the real picture so we can all be fair to each other.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
